  "_comment": "A task the owl sets aloud. `accepted` is matched against what on-device recognition heard, loosely — see QuestionMatcher. `reveal` is what the owl says when the answer was not on the list: it offers an answer of its own and moves on. There is no wrong, no score and no streak.",
  "_fallback": "`choices` is the no-recognition path: three cards the child taps instead of speaking. Because no child of three can read them and the illustrations are not drawn yet, the owl READS EACH CARD ALOUD while it lights up, and the child taps the one they heard. So a card is a spoken answer, not a picture name: for an animal-sound task the cards are sounds, not animals, because the question asked what sound it makes.",
